# Frontend Development Rules - Greek ERP/CRM System

## Core Technology Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15+ with App Router and TypeScript 5.3+
- **Styling**: ALWAYS use Tailwind CSS - never write custom CSS files
- **UI Components**: shadcn/ui as base component library
- **State Management**: Zustand for global state, React Query for server state
- **Forms**: React Hook Form with Zod validation
- **Icons**: Lucide React icons consistently

## Component Strategy

- **Reuse First**: Always check shared components before creating new ones
- **Extend shadcn/ui**: Build on existing base components
- **Greek Components**: Use AFMInput, DOYSelector, GreekPhoneInput for business data
- **Extract at 2+**: If pattern repeats twice, extract to shared component

## Styling Rules (MANDATORY)

- **Tailwind Only**: Never write custom CSS files or styled-components
- **Responsive**: Always include breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:)
- **Consistent Spacing**: Use standard spacing (p-4, m-6, space-y-4)
- **Theme Colors**: Use maritime color palette (#0066CC primary, #FFF700 accent)

## Form Standards

- **Pattern**: React Hook Form + Zod resolver for ALL forms
- **Validation**: Client-side validation with server sync
- **Greek Business**: Use specialized Greek validation components

## Internationalization (MANDATORY)

- **Strategy**: JSON files for static text, database for dynamic content
- **Languages**: Support Greek and English always
- **Translation**: Never hardcode text - use t('key') for everything
- **Namespaces**: Organize by module (crm:, erp:, common:)

## Greek Business Requirements

- **Validation**: Use Greek-specific components for AFM, DOY, phone numbers
- **AADE Integration**: Include status badges and compliance indicators
- **Formatting**: Greek date, currency, address formatting
- **VAT Calculations**: Location-aware Greek VAT rates

## Greek Reference Data Integration (MANDATORY)

- **Region Selector**: Use GreekRegionSelector for address forms - supports VAT zone detection
- **DOY Selector**: Use DOYSelector with autocomplete from master database
- **Legal Form Selector**: Use LegalFormSelector for company setup (AE, EPE, OE, EE, IKE, AT)
- **Bank Selector**: Use GreekBankSelector with SWIFT code validation
- **VAT Rate Calculator**: Use VATRateCalculator for context-aware rates (takeaway vs dine-in)
- **Business Activity**: Use KADSelector for business activity codes with hierarchy
- **Postal Code**: Use PostalCodeInput with geographic validation

## Data Handling

- **API Integration**: React Query for all server state
- **Loading States**: Use Skeleton components consistently
- **Error Handling**: Consistent error display patterns
- **Caching**: Leverage React Query caching strategies

## Security & Access Control

- **Permissions**: Use hasPermission() for conditional rendering
- **Company Isolation**: Respect multi-tenant boundaries
- **Greek Data**: Secure handling of AFM and business data

## Performance Standards

- **Optimization**: Memo expensive components, lazy load heavy ones
- **Bundle Size**: Code splitting for large components
- **Mobile**: Mobile-first responsive design
- **Accessibility**: ARIA attributes for all interactive elements

## File Organization

- **Structure**: ui/, shared/, greek/, forms/, layouts/
- **Naming**: PascalCase components, kebab-case files, camelCase hooks
- **Imports**: Explicit imports, no barrel exports for performance

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never write custom CSS files
- ❌ Don't hardcode text (always use i18n)
- ❌ Don't create components without checking shared library
- ❌ Don't skip responsive design
- ❌ Don't ignore Greek business validation
- ❌ Don't skip loading/error states
- ❌ Don't hardcode Greek reference data (regions, VAT rates, DOY codes) - use database
